not cleaned.","evidence_ids":["cmd-25c04b8859014aa3","cmd-af9e33e0b43c4831","cmd-360a706a957341c5","cmd-69dbb671a0ef4c0a","cmd-fe3c7b928f2241aa","cmd-d715d0a92cb04bb5","cmd-77d5d9aeecd8407e","cmd-ae48373de5bb48a1","cmd-f752a963cf3b4adf","cmd-fd35dca124904abc","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Both provider-wide restart protocols are complete: each node has a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, different post-restart boot identity, and recovered service/data state. The fixed lifecycle boot observations independently agree with those transitions. Hygiene is reduced modestly by two corrected implementation attempts and retained temporary evidence artifacts.","limitations":["Final preservation checks used SHA-1 while the authored baseline used SHA-256; preservation is supported by stable SHA-1 values throughout execution, early direct file-content observations, and the absence of commands modifying the supplied files, but there is no final same-algorithm SHA-256 comparison.","The lifecycle collector could not assess failed services because systemd is unsupported on this platform, and its yum package-health invocation only returned usage text. Direct service and platform checks therefore carry most of the final-state evidence.","The lifecycle listening-socket snapshots were empty and did not independently corroborate socket state; repeated executor netstat and connectivity probes supplied the direct listener evidence instead."]}
